			<div class="content" id="post-content-2665326">
									

<p>This is a bunch of disparate, random elements kind of thrown together without much regard for anything resembling an overall idea. Blade armed faceless humanoid with roots for feet turns people into street performers by poking them with her roots. This very much feels like something that came out of a random idea generator, and the problem with those is that there's no chance with those to make something that'll really affect a reader beyond &quot;huh, that's kind of weird, I guess.&quot;</p>
<p>I concur with Roget that the interview is filler; nothing in there gave us information beyond what could have been read already from the description. It suffers further from the fact that the exchange is kind of silly with the asking the subject their favorite color etc., and the dialogue is stilted and unnatural sounding.</p>

